\title{tidysynthesis: tidy meta-analysis and evidence synthesis}
\description{
tidysynthesis provides a pipe-friendly grammar for meta-analysis. Effect
sizes are computed with \code{\link[=meta_effect_size]{meta_effect_size()}}, pooled with \code{\link[=meta_pool]{meta_pool()}},
explained with \code{\link[=meta_regress]{meta_regress()}}, \code{\link[=meta_subgroup]{meta_subgroup()}} and
\code{\link[=meta_multilevel]{meta_multilevel()}}, compared across treatments with \code{\link[=meta_network]{meta_network()}},
checked for small-study effects with \code{\link[=meta_egger]{meta_egger()}}, \code{\link[=meta_begg]{meta_begg()}},
\code{\link[=meta_trimfill]{meta_trimfill()}}, \code{\link[=meta_pet_peese]{meta_pet_peese()}} and \code{\link[=meta_failsafe]{meta_failsafe()}}, and stress
tested with \code{\link[=meta_leave1out]{meta_leave1out()}}, \code{\link[=meta_cumulative]{meta_cumulative()}} and
\code{\link[=meta_influence]{meta_influence()}}. Every estimator is written in base R and
validated against published reference results.

Results are \code{tibble} subclasses that work with \code{dplyr}, \code{broom} style
tidiers (\code{\link[=tidy]{tidy()}}, \code{\link[=glance]{glance()}}, \code{\link[=augment]{augment()}}) and \code{\link[ggplot2:autoplot]{ggplot2::autoplot()}}.
The \code{tidymodels} integration includes \code{recipes} steps
(\code{\link[=step_meta_effect_size]{step_meta_effect_size()}}, \code{\link[=step_meta_precision]{step_meta_precision()}},
\code{\link[=step_meta_impute_sd]{step_meta_impute_sd()}}), \code{rsample} resampling schemes
(\code{\link[=meta_leave_study_out_cv]{meta_leave_study_out_cv()}}, \code{\link[=meta_cluster_cv]{meta_cluster_cv()}}), \code{yardstick} metrics
(\code{\link[=inverse_var_rmse]{inverse_var_rmse()}}, \code{\link[=coverage_prob]{coverage_prob()}}, \code{\link[=heterogeneity_r2]{heterogeneity_r2()}}) and a
\code{parsnip} model specification (\code{\link[=meta_linear]{meta_linear()}}).
}
